Frozen predecessor-writer fixture for #10637: a save taken by the pre-scheduler engine at Day of Judgment's first replacement choice: P1's Grizzly Bears (ObjectId 1) wears Hyena Umbra (2) and Spider Umbra (3), P0's Runeclaw Bear (4) has no choice. The member being asked sits AT the approval cursor (cursor 0) with its pause boundary, the shape the scheduler's checked restore upgrades to an explicit asking member.

Generated by the OLD serializer. Never regenerate it with a newer engine: its
value is that it is byte-for-byte what the predecessor engine wrote.

Generating commit: feedce4fce004d90dde693c28db8958dca65cce0
  (#10637's head before the live replacement-choice scheduler)

Serializer: PersistedGameState::capture(state) after state.capture_rng_word_pos(),
  pretty-printed with serde_json::to_string_pretty plus a trailing newline.

Command (bash, in a clean worktree checked out at the commit above, with the
generator below added as crates/engine/tests/integration/zz_feedce4fc_fixture_gen.rs
and a matching `mod zz_feedce4fc_fixture_gen;` line in shard_5.rs):

  CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 FIXTURE_DIR=/tmp/pr10637-gen \
  cargo test -p phase-engine --features proptest --test integration_5 generate_feedce4fc_fixtures -- --nocapture

One run writes both fixtures. Observed on that run:

